From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 04b0: pixel shader DXBC translation options: refactoringAllowed, fused mad, sample_b, loop-free forward control flow, IEEE multiplication (Direct3D 12; dxbc_ps_refactoring_allowed, dxbc_ps_mad, dxbc_sample_bias, dxbc_forward_cf, dxbc_ps_ieee_mul)

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (O3; changes R1-A, B, C, D and F of $WORK/scratch/R1/REPORT.md, whose variants/src is the working
  code of each). The DXBC translator they change is Xenia's (Triang3l, BSD-3-Clause) in the ReXGlue SDK. Not run in the game:
  built (SDK build of the series with this patch, scratch tree $WORK/scratch/O3) and run offline on the 1,061 translations of the
  E2 shader storage (the harness below), compiled by RGA for gfx1150, nothing more
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: R1 measured that a median MCLA pixel shader costs about 25 vector ALU instructions per Xenos instruction slot on the
  Radeon 880M (about 5 would do), from the way the DXBC translator emits it: the precise-mode flags, the SM3 "0 * anything = 0"
  check after every multiplication, no fused multiply-add, gradient-scaled sample_d where only the LOD bias is wanted, and a
  loop around the whole shader that survives in the biggest (forward-jump) ones. Five cvars, each its own option, all default
  false until a run has validated them (the profile turns them on). All of them are for pixel shaders only (vertex shaders are
  translated exactly as before: position invariance), and only on host render targets (the RTV path, not ROV); with all of them
  off the translation is byte-identical to the stock one (1,061 of 1,061 translations of the E2 corpus, 621 pixel and 440 vertex).
  * dxbc_ps_refactoring_allowed (R1-A): sets the refactoringAllowed global flag (dcl_globalFlags) in a pixel shader that writes
    neither oDepth nor, through depth_stencil_mode, the float24 conversion of the depth, so the driver compiles it in fast math
    mode (fused multiply-add, reassociation, uniform integer work of the fetch constants on the scalar unit). Last-ulp colour
    differences only. RGA, 126 pixel shaders (R1's subset: all 52 jmp ones, every 8th other, the tone map): vector ALU -20.2% (280,161 -> 223,551),
    VGPRs mean 78.4 -> 62.3.
  * dxbc_ps_mad (R1-B, only together with dxbc_ps_refactoring_allowed): the Xenos mad, and the dp2add/dp3/dp4 terms after the
    first, are the DXBC mad (one fused multiply-add) instead of mul + the SM3 zero check + add. THIS DROPS THE SM3 CHECK FOR THESE
    (0 * infinity and 0 * NaN in them are NaN, not 0): the same risk as dxbc_ps_ieee_mul, only for these instructions. RGA, on top
    of A: -29.7% in total (196,880), mean VGPRs 61.2.
  * dxbc_sample_bias (R1-D): where the LOD is computed by the hardware (no gradients from registers, mip filtering on) the texture
    is sampled with sample_b, the bias (fetch constant + register LOD + instruction bias, as before) being its operand, instead of
    sample_d with the coarse derivatives made by hand and multiplied by 2^bias: the same LOD (the gradients times 2^b are the LOD
    plus b, also with the anisotropic filter, whose ratio the scale leaves alone), no derivative instructions, 4 address
    registers fewer per sample. Not for 3D / stacked fetches (the second layer of a stacked texture is sampled under a per-pixel
    `if`, which implicit derivatives would be taken in; the stock translation takes the derivatives before it). New opcode
    sample_b (74) in format/dxbc.h. RGA alone: -6.6% (261,798), mean VGPRs 77.3.
  * dxbc_forward_cf (R1-F): a pixel shader whose control flow is execs and forward jumps only (at least one jmp; no loop, call or
    return; the new Shader::control_flow_forward_jumps_only, found in AnalyzeUcode, which for MCLA are 23 shaders, 52 pixel
    translations, the biggest ones) is translated without the `loop` around everything: the code of a label is the if (pc <= label)
    region of the stock non-switch flow, and a jmp or an end sets pc (the end to the maximum) and closes the region, opening the
    rest of it for the lanes that haven't jumped or ended (pc <= the region's label), so nothing needs to jump back and the
    compiler keeps no loop back-edge. Same per-lane semantics as the stock translation. RGA alone: on the 52 jmp translations vector ALU -1.2%, mean VGPRs 121.9 -> 106.1 (-13%), the backward branches of the ISA 60 -> 0.
  * dxbc_ps_ieee_mul (R1-C, risky): no SM3 "+-0 or denormal times anything is +0" in mul, mad, dp#, dst, muls, mulsc and mulsprev
    (the min/eq/movc after each multiplication): plain IEEE multiplication, so 0 * infinity and 0 * NaN are NaN, which can leave
    NaN pixels (bloom, TAA smears) where the game relies on the zero. RGA alone: -27.0% (204,489), mean VGPRs 64.5. Needs a frozen-frame picture diff
    before the profile turns it on.
  All five together: RGA vector ALU -48.3% (280,161 -> 144,969), VGPRs mean 78.4 -> 56.7 (the 52 jmp translations 121.9 -> 82.5, vector ALU -47.0%) (the same 126).
  What the cvars key: the options are not read by the translation but are bits of the pixel shader modification
  (DxbcShaderTranslator::Modification::pixel: ps_refactoring_allowed, ps_mad, sample_bias, forward_cf, ps_ieee_mul, in the free
  upper half of the second dword), set by DxbcShaderTranslator::ApplyPixelShaderOptimizations from the cvars when a draw makes
  its modification (PipelineCache::GetCurrentPixelShaderModification, host render targets only) and only where the option has an
  effect on the shader (not for one writing depth; sample_bias with a texture; forward_cf with forward jumps). The modification
  is the key of the translation (Shader::translations_), of the pipeline (PipelineDescription.pixel_shader_modification, hashed)
  and of the stored pipeline description (.xpso), so a combination of the cvars never reuses the DXBC, the pipeline or the stored
  description of another one, however and whenever a cvar is changed (they are hot-reloadable: a change makes new translations and
  pipelines, compiled on first use). All bits 0 is the stock modification, so the stored descriptions of older runs stay valid
  (the Modification::kVersion and the storage versions are unchanged) and the shader storage (.xsh, ucode only) is not affected.
  At the start-up preload, a stored pixel shader description whose options differ from the current cvars' (computed per shader after
  its ucode analysis, the same function) is not translated and so its pipeline is not made: the file keeps the entries of every
  combination, and a run builds only its own. A new combination compiles its pipelines on first use (like any new shader), so the
  first run after a toggle stutters once.
Bucket: REDO

04b0-dxbc-ps-optimizations.patch (mcla-x86 O3; R1 of $WORK/scratch/R1/REPORT.md)

Changed files: include/rex/graphics/format/dxbc.h (sample_b), include/rex/graphics/pipeline/shader/{dxbc_translator.h
(Modification::pixel bits, ApplyPixelShaderOptimizations, the option accessors, SplitForwardControlFlowRegion,
cf_forward_region_start_), shader.h (control_flow_forward_jumps_only)}, src/graphics/pipeline/shader/{dxbc_translator.cpp (the cvars,
ApplyPixelShaderOptimizations, the global flag, the forward control flow), dxbc_translator_alu.cpp (mad, ieee mul),
dxbc_translator_fetch.cpp (sample_b), translator.cpp (the control flow analysis)}, src/graphics/d3d12/pipeline_cache.cpp (the
modification and the preload skip). No new files; Vulkan untouched.

Checks done (scratch tree $WORK/scratch/O3 = series 90 + this patch):
  * python tools/prepare_sdk.py --work $WORK/scratch/O3 build (Release): builds and installs; clang++ 20.1.8, no new warning in the
