  * Harness (scratch/O3/harness/harness_o3.cpp: R1's harness, with the cvars from its command line applied by
    ApplyPixelShaderOptimizations, linked with the objects of that build) over the 1,061 (shader, modification) pairs of the E2
    storage, AMD, bindless, RTV: all cvars off: 1,061 of 1,061 byte-identical to the stock translation (R1's out/). Each option on
    alone against R1's variant of it (harness_v2 with R1_REFACT, R1_REFACT + R1_MAD, R1_TEXBIAS, R1_NOZM): pixel shaders
    byte-identical except two translations (the one shader that writes oDepth, which A leaves alone). The forward flow differs from
    R1's `f` as intended (R1's removed the loop from every loop-free shader, this one only from the 52 jmp translations, and
    splits the region after an end too); vertex shaders differ from R1's variants as intended (R1's applied to them).
  * RGA 2.15, DX12 live driver, gfx1150, 126 pixel shaders each with its vertex shader, run under the heavy lock: every variant
    compiled (0 failed); the numbers above (vector ALU = the ISA
    instructions v_*, VGPRs from the RGA statistics); A and A+B have the same ISA totals as R1's variants r and rm, all five within 0.02% of
    R1's fa (A + mad + sample_b + C + loop-free flow), D alone -6.6% where R1 measured -8.4% on top of the others.
  * Not run: the game, a picture, the stored-pipeline preload and the pipeline creation (they need the SDK in the game: next
    paragraph).

Checks to run (VER), in this order (each is a profile cvar: dxbc_ps_refactoring_allowed=true dxbc_ps_mad=true dxbc_sample_bias=true
dxbc_forward_cf=true, dxbc_ps_ieee_mul=true last):
  1. All five false: the pipeline storage and the picture as before (nothing in the log about the options).
  2. dxbc_ps_refactoring_allowed=true: no shader or pipeline creation failures in the log; a frozen frame against the stock one (last-ulp
     differences only: a difference image of a few levels at most); GPU time of the draws (n1080 A/B pair).
  3. + dxbc_ps_mad, + dxbc_sample_bias, + dxbc_forward_cf: the same, one at a time. dxbc_sample_bias: textures at oblique angles
     and bias (the fetch constants with LOD bias) look the same (mip transitions identical to a stock frame); dxbc_forward_cf: the
     52 forward-jump pixel shaders (the world and car materials) give the same picture.
  4. dxbc_ps_ieee_mul=true: frozen frame diff for NaN / black or white pixels, bloom, TAA, rain and reflections.
  5. A toggle between runs on the same cache: "Created N graphics pipelines ... from the storage" counts only the pipelines of the
